@startuml Admin_Photobooth_Management_SSD

actor "Administrator" as Admin
participant "UI: Photobooth Management" as UI
participant "Database" as DB
participant "S3 Storage" as S3

== View Filters ==

Admin -> UI: Access photobooth page
activate UI

UI -> DB: Fetch active filters
activate DB
DB --> UI: Return active filters
deactivate DB

UI -> DB: Fetch archived filters
activate DB
DB --> UI: Return archived filters
deactivate DB

UI --> Admin: Display filters (Active/Archived tabs)
deactivate UI

== Add Filter ==

Admin -> UI: Enter filter details (name, category, image)
activate UI

UI -> UI: Validate input

alt Input valid
    UI --> Admin: Show confirmation dialog
    Admin -> UI: Confirm add
    
    alt Image is file upload
        UI -> S3: Upload image
        activate S3
        S3 --> UI: Return S3 URL
        deactivate S3
    else Image is URL
        UI -> UI: Use provided URL
    end
    
    UI -> DB: Save filter record
    activate DB
    DB --> UI: Filter created
    deactivate DB
    
    UI --> Admin: Show success, refresh list
else Input invalid
    UI --> Admin: Show validation errors
end

deactivate UI

== Edit Filter ==

Admin -> UI: Click "Edit" on filter
activate UI

UI --> Admin: Display form with current data

Admin -> UI: Modify details and submit
UI --> Admin: Show confirmation dialog
Admin -> UI: Confirm update

alt New image uploaded
    UI -> S3: Delete old image
    activate S3
    deactivate S3
    
    UI -> S3: Upload new image
    activate S3
    S3 --> UI: Return new S3 URL
    deactivate S3
end

UI -> DB: Update filter record
activate DB
DB --> UI: Filter updated
deactivate DB

UI --> Admin: Show success, refresh list
deactivate UI

== Archive Filter ==

Admin -> UI: Click "Archive"
activate UI

UI --> Admin: Show confirmation dialog
Admin -> UI: Confirm archive

UI -> DB: Update filter status (archived: true)
activate DB
DB --> UI: Filter archived
deactivate DB

UI --> Admin: Refresh lists
deactivate UI

== Restore Filter ==

Admin -> UI: Switch to Archived tab
activate UI

Admin -> UI: Click "Restore"
UI --> Admin: Show confirmation dialog
Admin -> UI: Confirm restore

UI -> DB: Update filter status (archived: false)
activate DB
DB --> UI: Filter restored
deactivate DB

UI --> Admin: Refresh lists
deactivate UI

== Delete Filter ==

Admin -> UI: Click "Delete" on archived filter
activate UI

UI --> Admin: Show warning dialog
Admin -> UI: Confirm delete

UI -> S3: Delete image from S3
activate S3
deactivate S3

UI -> DB: Remove filter record
activate DB
DB --> UI: Filter deleted
deactivate DB

UI --> Admin: Refresh archived list
deactivate UI

@enduml
